    <div class="section-header">INSTRUCTIONS TO BIDDERS</div>
    <p>Questions: Questions regarding this bid will be accepted up to five (5) calendar days prior to the bid opening. Please email all questions to the buyer shown above or <a href="http://www.nmt.edu/purchasing-services">purchasing@nmt.edu</a>.</p>
    <p>Please read carefully all instructions, specifications, terms and conditions. Failure to comply may result in the submitted bid being declared non-responsive.</p>
    <p>Type or print all information requested in this bid in the spaces provided in the bid package. Any corrections made should be initialed. The bid must contain an original, inked signature and one (1) copy of the bid. Bids must be submitted in a sealed envelope or sealed package and clearly display the name and address of BIDDER, this BID NUMBER, DUE DATE, BID OPENING TIME and marked as "SEALED BID" on the front of the envelope or package. Each bid must be addressed and submitted separately, i.e., not to be included with sample packages or other numbered bids. FAILED OR MISREAD BIDS ARE NOT ACCEPTABLE. Late bids will be rejected and returned to the SENDER UNOPENED. The time and date stamped by the date/time clock in the Purchasing Services Office shall determine the "Official Due Date and Time" regarding this bid.</p>
    <p>Bids received by the established date and time will be opened publicly. The opening will be held in the NMMT Purchasing Services Office. Anyone may attend the opening. All information will become public information at the time the bid is opened.</p>
    <p>All bids shall be firm for acceptance for sixty (60) days from the date of the bid opening unless specified otherwise.</p>
    <p>Note: Only bids received for these items will be considered. Quotes submitted to a department by a vendor prior to the bid issue date are considered null and void by NMMT.</p>
    <p>New Mexico Tech Federal Identification Number: <span data-field="nmt_fed_id">{{ nmt_fed_id }}</span> New Mexico CRS Number: <span data-field="nmt_crs_id">{{ nmt_crs_id }}</span></p>
    <p>DUE TO THE GEOGRAPHIC LOCATION OF NEW MEXICO TECH, OVERNIGHT OR EXPRESS DELIVERY SERVICES ARE INCREASINGLY EXPERIENCING LATE DELIVERY TO CAMPUS. ALTHOUGH THESE SERVICES GUARANTEE THE DELIVERY WILL ARRIVE IN A TIMELY MANNER, OFTEN IT DOES NOT. IT FALLS UPON THE BIDDER OR OFFEROR TO ENSURE THEIR PACKAGE IS SENT WITH SUFFICIENT LEAD TIME TO ENSURE DELIVERY BEFORE THE DATE AND TIME SHOWN IN THE BID.</p>
</div>

<div class="page">
    <div class="section-header">STANDARD BID TERMS AND CONDITIONS</div>
    <ol>
        <li><strong>GENERAL:</strong> When the Buyer for the New Mexico Institute of Mining and Technology (New Mexico Tech) issues a purchase document in response to Supplier's bid, a binding contract is created governed by the laws of the State of New Mexico and consisting of Supplier's bid and New Mexico Tech's purchase document. The terms and conditions of the purchase document shall be resolved in the following descending order of precedence: (a) order-specific provisions which are typed or handwritten by New Mexico Tech on the purchase document; (b) documents executed by New Mexico Tech incorporated by reference on the face page(s) of the purchase document; (c) these Standard Terms and Conditions; (d) any Statement of Work (SOW) attached to the purchase document; and (e) any specifications and other specifications attached to the purchase document.</li>
        <li><strong>ACCEPTANCE:</strong> New Mexico Tech reserves the right to accept or reject any and all bids, to waive any irregularity, and to accept any part of a bid as deemed to be in the best interest of New Mexico Tech.</li>
        <li><strong>ACKNOWLEDGEMENT OF AMENDMENT / ADDENDUM:</strong> Bidders shall acknowledge receipt of any amendments / addendums to this bid by identifying the amendment number and date in the space provided in the bid package.</li>
        <li><strong>ALTERNATE BID ITEMS:</strong> The Manufacturer and Model Numbers furnished on the itemized list, or in the specifications, are for identification purposes only. The standard of performance and characteristics desired and not intended to limit or restrict competition. Offers submitted as equal alternatives will be considered provided adequate descriptive literature is submitted. The Buyer reserves the right to reject any item(s) not meeting specifications or less than equal in performance and characteristics to the items specified. The determination of equivalency of like items is at the sole discretion of New Mexico Tech.</li>
        <li><strong>APPROPRIATION:</strong> The performance of this Agreement by NMMT is contingent upon availability of sufficient funds and sufficient appropriations and authorizations have been made. NMMT shall not be liable for any failure to make such performance. NMMT's decision as to whether sufficient funds are available and whether sufficient appropriations and authorizations have been made shall be made in good faith and in its sole discretion, shall be accepted unconditionally by the Contractor.</li>
        <li><strong>CANCELLATION:</strong> New Mexico Tech reserves the right to cancel any request for bid, purchase order or contract, in whole or in part, without penalty, due to non-appropriation of funds, or for failure of the Supplier to comply with the terms, conditions or specifications or when in the best interest of New Mexico Tech.</li>
        <li><strong>DELIVERY:</strong> Please state your earliest delivery date in the area provided in the bid package.</li>
        <li><strong>DELIVERY DELAYS:</strong> If after award, the Supplier becomes aware of a possible problem that could cause a delay agreed to delivery schedule, the Supplier must immediately notify the Buyer. Notification may be electronic or via telephone, giving New Mexico Tech a reasonable alternative action.</li>
        <li><strong>DISCOUNTS & PAYMENT TERMS:</strong> In determination of award, discounts for equally rated bids will not be used in computing the low bid. Payment terms and discount time will be computed from the date of satisfactory receipt of the item/services, or a contractually agreed upon invoice, whichever is later. The point of receipt shall be the delivery address for shipments, or the billing address for invoices, as specified on the purchase order.</li>
        <li><strong>E-VERIFICATION:</strong> The Immigration Reform and Control Act of 1986, Pub L 90-603 (8 USC 1324) requires employers to verify the eligibility of individuals for employment. The Buyer requires that the Supplier provide documentation to prove that all individuals hired to work in the United States are authorized to work in the United States. This information will be used by employers to comply with federal law and will be made available for inspection by authorized officials of the Department of Homeland Security, Department of Labor, and other federal agencies.</li>
        <li><strong>SUBMISSIONS OF SAMPLES / DRAWINGS / LITERATURE:</strong> It may be necessary to test samples or drawings or literature. All samples, drawings, or literature shall be furnished free of expense to New Mexico Tech. Returns shall only be made at the Bidder's request and expense.</li>
        <li><strong>TAXES:</strong> New Mexico Tech is exempt from New Mexico Sales Taxes on services and goods purchased for construction. Services provided to New Mexico Tech as a separate line item and not included in the bidder's base price bid. For state reporting purposes,</li>
    </ol>

